3 page 29 and 30 (examples)

Reading these examples, I had a thought on Group indexes vs element indexes.

I propose we create a notation to communicate differences between element indexes, group indexes and parameters.
In reading these examples, there is a lot of non-useful ambiguity.

Maybe instead of just using number 1 2 3 etc... we should use something like:
group-1, instr-elem-1 etc, so that it is always 100% clear what is being referred to.
So when group indexes are created by alea, they don't create
1 2 3 1, but they create G1, G2, G3, G1.
If these group indexes are of a particular parameter, that should also be explicit.
We will need to think how we express this, but it is very important for being able to think about examples in PR2.






